<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore June retail sales rise 1.5 pct on year.</title>
<headline>Singapore June retail sales rise 1.5 pct on year.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's retail sales index (base 1991) rose 1.5 percent in June compared to a year ago, the Statistics Department said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The index was also up 1.5 percent compared with May.</p>
<p>Excluding motor vehicles, the index registered a month-on-month gain of 2.2 percent in June.</p>
<p>Total June retail sales were estimated at Singapore $2.088 billion.</p>
<p>The report said that year-on-year, in constant prices, the retail index rose by 4.6 percent.  </p>
<p>					 Month-on-month     Yr-on-yr</p>
<p>    Total index			    1.5		 1.5</p>
<p>    X-vehicle sales			2.2		 5.8</p>
<p>    Textiles/apparels		   -1.2		 0.1</p>
<p>    Furniture/household equipment   15.1		20.5</p>
<p>    Motor vehicles			-1.3	     -12.8</p>
<p>    Petrol stations		     -4.0		 0.1</p>
<p>    Department stores/supermarkets   5.0		 7.7</p>
<p>    General provisions		  -3.3		 3.3</p>
<p>    Other retail			  -1.9		 2.4</p>
